Homework Hack: JSON Character Sheet
Task
Create a character sheet using a JavaScript object.
Your character sheet must contain:
name
username
character_info
level
class
health
skills
Then:
Access and display the properties.
Convert the object into a JSON string.
Print the JSON string.
Parse the JSON string back into an object.
Print the parsed object.
Solution Skeleton
%%js

// CODE_RUNNER: Create a character sheet and convert it to JSON.

// 1. Create your JavaScript object.

const character_sheet = {
    name: "",
    username: "",
    character_info: {
        level: "",
        class: "",
        health: ""
    },
    skills: []
};

// 2. Access and display properties.

// Write your code here.



// 3. Convert the JavaScript object to a JSON string.

const jsonString = JSON.stringify(character_sheet);

console.log("JSON string:");
console.log(jsonString);


// 4. Parse the JSON string back into a JavaScript object.

const parsedCharacterSheet = JSON.parse(jsonString);

console.log("Parsed character sheet:");
console.log(parsedCharacterSheet);

